  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection and winter assistance for Afghan households</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this UNHCR project is to provide vulnerable Afghan households with timely winter assistance, including heating, warm clothing, health services, documentation support, and gender-based violence (GBV) protection in harsh winter locations. This project provides heating/fuel support and winter clothing, among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 101,429 people, including 21,301 women, 22,315 men, 57,813 children, and 15,651 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
